From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clavin <clavin@electronjs.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:24:04 -0700
Subject: Update tzdata to 2026d

Brings ICU's time zone data up to tzdata 2026d, matching upstream ICU's
6ebb40c5 ("Update tzdata to 2026c and rebuild data files.") and 5aa52620
("Update TZDB to 2024d", which is 2026d despite its subject). Zones whose
offsets change include America/Vancouver (permanent UTC-7 from 2026-11-01),
America/Edmonton, America/Inuvik, Africa/Casablanca and Africa/El_Aaiun.

Chromium picks up time zone updates by rolling ICU in its DEPS, which this
Chromium branch has not done. Upstream's common/icudtl.dat also carries
unrelated data changes, so rather than copying it whole, this patch replaces
only its time zone items (metaZones.res, timezoneTypes.res and
zoneinfo64.res) with upstream's, keeping every other item and the existing
layout. Making the same replacement in upstream 8cc91d9b6, the parent of the
tzdata roll, reproduces upstream 5aa52620's common/icudtl.dat byte for byte.

The source/data/misc text files are upstream's at 5aa52620. Only
common/icudtl.dat is rebuilt since it is the only ICU data file Electron
uses.

This patch can be removed once Chromium's DEPS pins ICU at or after
5aa52620.

diff --git a/README.chromium b/README.chromium
index ac256fc7519781a50d040e0b0ec6a1c79438b549..88e5467d0f5009ffbaa4eb4b9e78be43771e378c 100644
--- a/README.chromium
+++ b/README.chromium
@@ -208,9 +208,9 @@ D. Local Modifications
     bug: https://crbug.com/381620359
     (scripts/update_tz.sh offers to perform this patch automatically)
 
-  As of Feb 25, 2026, the latest version is 2025c
+  As of Sep 24, 2026, the latest version is 2026d
   and the above files are available at the ICU github repos.
-  Compare: https://lists.iana.org/hyperkitty/list/tz-announce@iana.org/thread/TAGXKYLMAQRZRFTERQ33CEKOW7KRJVAK/
+  Compare: https://lists.iana.org/hyperkitty/list/tz-announce@iana.org/thread/L4IGHJRBUQR53F7RTEHM5IS7ZMBR3YXP/
 
 4. Build-related changes
 
